{
  "2Kings.13.11.1-m.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2022.12.07 - Changes.xml, date: 2022.09.01, number: 15 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Kings_2 13:11.1</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Kings_2 13:11.1</h1>\n  <h2>Change hataf-patah under ayin to patah. Change merkha under shin to meteg. Add note 'm'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2022.12.07 - Changes/images/2022.09.01/15-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The vertical line under the shin lacks sufficient northeast-to-southwest inclination to be transcribed as a merkha.</p>\n  <p>The BHL has a patah then meteg under yod, a hataf-patah under the ayin, and a segol then merkha under the shin \n                           (as shown in the Reference text above); \n                           BHL Appendix A has no entries for this word. </p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2022.12.07 - Changes/2022.12.07 - Changes.xml?2022.09.01-15\">2022.12.07 - Changes.xml : 2022.09.01-15</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?m\">All \"This meteg is a merkha in other texts.\" ('m') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "2Kings.13.17.6-t.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2022.12.07 - Changes.xml, date: 2022.08.14, number: 8 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Kings_2 13:17.6</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Kings_2 13:17.6</h1>\n  <h2>Remove mahapakh from under yod. Place qadma on yod.  Add  note 't'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2022.12.07 - Changes/images/2022.08.14/8-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>Although LC text has a smudge extending partly under the yod, it is unlikely that there is an accent under the yod.\n                A diagonal, southeast-to-northwest blurr occurs at the top tip of the yod. \n                This could be a qadma, providing a primary accent on the word.</p>\n  <p>The Hebrew Wikisource Miqra According to the Masorah (23 Sep 2022) has a qadma on the yod.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Moshe Greenberg</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2022.12.07 - Changes/2022.12.07 - Changes.xml?2022.08.14-8\">2022.12.07 - Changes.xml : 2022.08.14-8</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "2Kings.14.6.7-t.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2022.12.07 - Changes.xml, date: 2022.09.01, number: 17 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Kings_2 14:6.7</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Kings_2 14:6.7</h1>\n  <h2>Replace munah under samekh with meteg. Add note 't'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2022.12.07 - Changes/images/2022.09.01/17-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The vertical line under the samekh has a slight northwest-to-southeast inclination \n                      and might be transcribed as a tipeha. A tipeha is unexpected here, however.</p>\n  <p>An erasure appears to have occurred at the lower, left corner of the line under the samekh.\n                      This erasure might have been of the horizontal line of a munah. \n                      The vertical line of a munah has a slight northwest-to-southeast inclination and\n                          if the horizontal line of a munah is erased, the result would have the shape shown in the image;\n                             a slightly inclined meteg.\n                      The immediately preceding word, on the preceding line, has a munah.\n                      The accent under the samekh is transcribed here as a meteg reflecting this possibility \n                          and marked with a 't' note. \n                </p>\n  <p>The BHL has meteg under the samekh; BHL Appendix A has no entries for this word. </p>\n  <p>\n                      Ben Denckla: Breuer-DM reveals that there is a tradition, \n                         attested in the Cairo Codex of the Prophets and other sources, \n                             of having munaḥ-space on this word (בְּסֵ֣פֶר) \n                                 instead of meteg-maqaf (בְּסֵֽפֶר־). \n                </p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2022.12.07 - Changes/2022.12.07 - Changes.xml?2022.09.01-17\">2022.12.07 - Changes.xml : 2022.09.01-17</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "2Kings.14.8.1-t.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2022.12.07 - Changes.xml, date: 2022.09.01, number: 18 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Kings_2 14:8.1</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Kings_2 14:8.1</h1>\n  <h2>Markings on aleph are unclear. Add note 't'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2022.12.07 - Changes/images/2022.09.01/18-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The ink on this word is flaking off.</p>\n  <p>The BHL has a qamats then munah under the aleph; BHL Appendix A has no entries for this word. </p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2022.12.07 - Changes/2022.12.07 - Changes.xml?2022.09.01-18\">2022.12.07 - Changes.xml : 2022.09.01-18</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "2Kings.17.4.20-t.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2023.04.01 - Changes.xml, date: 2023.01.31, number: 1 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Kings_2 17:4.20</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Kings_2 17:4.20</h1>\n  <h2>Replace patah under ayin with sheva. Add note 't'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2023.04.01 - Changes/images/2023.01.31/1-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>\n                    The text quality is poor. \n                    Neither a patah or sheva marking is clear; though a sheva is more evident.\n                    The size of this sheva is significantly smaller than that on the following tsadi.\n                </p>\n  <p>\n                    BHL has a sheva under the ayin.\n                    BHL Appendix A makes no comment on this verse.\n                </p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Anonymous</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2023.04.01 - Changes/2023.04.01 - Changes.xml?2023.01.31-1\">2023.04.01 - Changes.xml : 2023.01.31-1</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "2Kings.18.27.21-c.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2021.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2021.08.07, number: 20 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Kings_2 18:27.21</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Kings_2 18:27.21</h1>\n  <h2>Word lacks accent, add note 'c'; MAM ends the word with a Maqaf (  ס־  ).</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2021.10.19 - Changes/images/2021.08.07/20-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Ben Denckla</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2021.10.19 - Changes/2021.10.19 - Changes.xml?2021.08.07-20\">2021.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2021.08.07-20</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?c\">All \"Text is correct relative to LC. Usually this marks a peculiarity of the LC relative to the other Masoretic texts.\" ('c') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "2Kings.19.37.9-q.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2024.04.15, number: 25 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Kings_2 19:37.9</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Kings_2 19:37.9</h1>\n  <h2>Remove unsupported dagesh from bet in qere without ketiv word. Add note 'q'. [בָּנָיו֙]</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/images/2024.04.15/25-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The image shows words 8 and 10 of the UXLC text. Word 9 is marked as a qere without ketiv in the right margin and given as בניו. The markings qamats, qamats, pashta, are seen between the two words in the image. These markings are intended for the qere. No dagesh is indicated for the bet. It will be removed and a transcription note added,</p>\n  <p>BHL has a dagesh in the bet in the qere word, בָּנָיו֙. BHL doesn't show a dagesh in its ketiv body text markings. BHLA has no entry for this verse.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>CVK</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes.xml?2024.04.15-25\">2024.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2024.04.15-25</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?q\">All \"UXLC differs from the conventional word for the qere.\" ('q') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "2Kings.20.18.8-q.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2024.04.15, number: 26 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Kings_2 20:18.8</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Kings_2 20:18.8</h1>\n  <h2>Replace unsupported dagesh in vav with a qubuts under het in qere word. Add note 'q'. [יִקָּ֑חוּ]</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/images/2024.04.15/26-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The qere word, יקחו, in the right margin, ends in a vav. This vav is not present in the ketiv body text, יקח. A qubuts vowel is present under the he. A small dagesh for the qof is in the upper part of the qof loop.</p>\n  <p>BHL has a dagesh in the qof and has a dagesh (acting as a shuruq dot) in the vav, יִקָּ֑חוּ.  BHLA has no entry for this verse.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>CVK</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes.xml?2024.04.15-26\">2024.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2024.04.15-26</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?q\">All \"UXLC differs from the conventional word for the qere.\" ('q') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "2Kings.21.26.1-c.html": "<html>\n<header profile=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/11/profile\" > \n        <meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/> \n        <title>2 Kings 21:26.1</title>\n</header>\n    \n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n        <h1>2 Kings 21:26.1</h1>\n        <h4>The LC contains the unusual markings on the bet.</h4>\n        \n        <table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5pt\"><tr><td>\n            <center>\n                <img src=\"../../Changes/2021.10.19 - Changes/images/2021.05.19/6-Detail.jpg\" border=\"4pt\"/>\n            </center>\n        </td></tr>\n        <p/>\n        <tr><td>\n            <center><i>Credit: Sefaria.org.\n            </i></center>\n        </td></tr>\n        </table>\n        <p/>\n        A sheva and a holam on a consonant is unusual.\n        <p/>\n        <b><i>Ben Denckla</i></b>\n        <p/>\n        <p align=\"right\"><b>2021.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2021.05.19-6</b></p>\n        <p/>\n        <table border=\"1pt\" align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"16pt\">\n            <tr><td>\n              <span style=\"color:blue;font-size:14pt\">\n                  <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?c\">All \"Text is correct\" ('c') notes</a>\n              </span>\n              <p/>\n              <span style=\"color:blue;font-size:14pt\">\n                  <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n              </span>\n            </td?</tr>\n        </table>\n        <p/>\n        </body>\n</html>\n",
  "2Kings.23.12.16-t.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2022.12.07 - Changes.xml, date: 2022.09.01, number: 22 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Kings_2 23:12.16</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Kings_2 23:12.16</h1>\n  <h2>Replace zaqef-qatan above shin with revia. Add note 't'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2022.12.07 - Changes/images/2022.09.01/22-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>A faint blurr above the left-most dot above the shin may have made the accent a zaqef-qatan.\n                   The accent will be transcribed as a revia.</p>\n  <p>The BHL has a revia above the shin; BHL Appendix A has no entries for this word. </p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2022.12.07 - Changes/2022.12.07 - Changes.xml?2022.09.01-22\">2022.12.07 - Changes.xml : 2022.09.01-22</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "2Kings.24.10.4-q.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2024.04.12, number: 2 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Kings_2 24:10.4</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Kings_2 24:10.4</h1>\n  <h2>Replace unsupported dagesh on vav with qubuts under lamed. Add note 'q'. [ועָל֗וּ]</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/images/2024.04.12/2-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>Example from BHL \"Qere and Ketiv\", p. xx, on qubuts (qibbuṣ) to mark a dagesh in the qere. The ketiv body text is עלה; the qere in the right margin is עלו. In the image the qubuts is positioned under the between the ayin and the lamed.</p>\n  <p>BHL has a dagesh (acting as a shuruq dot) in the vav, ועָל֗וּ. BHLA has no entry for this verse.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>CVK</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes.xml?2024.04.12-2\">2024.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2024.04.12-2</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?q\">All \"UXLC differs from the conventional word for the qere.\" ('q') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "2Kings.4.3.11-q.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2024.04.15, number: 22 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Kings_2 4:3.11</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Kings_2 4:3.11</h1>\n  <h2>Remove unsupported sheva from final kaf in qere word. Add note 'q'. [שְׁכֵנָ֑יִךְ]</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/images/2024.04.15/22-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The qere in the left margin is  שכניך; the ketiv body text, שכנכי. That is, the two qere/ketiv letters yod and kaf are interchanged. Thus the marking under the ketiv kaf is intended for the qere yod; no marking is present under the ketiv yod; thus a sheva should not be added to the qere final kaf.</p>\n  <p>BHL has a hiriq on the yod and a sheva on the final kaf in the qere, שְׁכֵנָ֑יִךְ.  BHLA has no entry for this verse.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>CVK</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes.xml?2024.04.15-22\">2024.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2024.04.15-22</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?q\">All \"UXLC differs from the conventional word for the qere.\" ('q') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "2Kings.6.25.17-q.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2024.04.15, number: 23 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Kings_2 6:25.17</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Kings_2 6:25.17</h1>\n  <h2>Remove unsupported dagesh from dalet in qere word. Add note 'q'. [דִּבְיוֹנִ֖ים]</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/images/2024.04.15/23-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The qere in the right margin, דביונים, differs in two letters from the ketiv body text, חרייונים. The initial letter is a het and the yod is doubled in the ketiv. The qere has a dalet as the initial letter and a single yod. The het in the ketiv body text lacks a dagesh but has a hiriq. Thus, a dagesh on the qere dalet is unsupported. Dotan's assertion (pg. xx) that the writer will not place a dagesh in a letter not taking a dagesh, even in the ketiv form, may be in action here. The holam is over the 4-th letter in the ketiv body text; thus it belongs to the 4-th letter of the qere, a vav.</p>\n  <p>BHL has a dagesh in the dalet and a holam on the vav in the qere, דִּבְיוֹנִ֖ים.  BHLA has no entry for this verse.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>CVK</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes.xml?2024.04.15-23\">2024.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2024.04.15-23</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?q\">All \"UXLC differs from the conventional word for the qere.\" ('q') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "2Kings.9.14.18-m.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2022.12.07 - Changes.xml, date: 2022.09.01, number: 11 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Kings_2 9:14.18</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Kings_2 9:14.18</h1>\n  <h2>Change tipeha under aleph to meteg. Add note 'm'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2022.12.07 - Changes/images/2022.09.01/11-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The vertical line under the aleph lacks sufficient northeast-to-southwest inclination to be transcribed as a merkha.</p>\n  <p>The BHL has a merkha under the aleph, not a tipeha. \n                           BHL Appendix A has no entry for this word. \n                </p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2022.12.07 - Changes/2022.12.07 - Changes.xml?2022.09.01-11\">2022.12.07 - Changes.xml : 2022.09.01-11</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?m\">All \"This meteg is a merkha in other texts.\" ('m') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "2Kings.9.17.19-m.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2022.12.07 - Changes.xml, date: 2022.09.01, number: 12 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Kings_2 9:17.19</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Kings_2 9:17.19</h1>\n  <h2>Replace sheva on shin with patah. Add 't' note. \n                         Replace merkha on lamed with meteg. Add 'm' note.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2022.12.07 - Changes/images/2022.09.01/12-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The vowel under the shin is hard to determine. \n                      A patah is a better fit than a sheva. \n                </p>\n  <p>\n                      A blob emerges from the top of the lamed of a word on the following line; \n                          word 22 of this verse. \n                      The blob might be considered in determining the markings on the shin of this word, word 19. \n                      There is a similar blob emerging from the lamed of the 5-th word of this verse. \n                      Consequently, the blob is considered to be an odd part of the lamed of word 22 \n                          and not part of the markings on the shin of word 19.\n                </p>\n  <p>The BHL has a hataf patah under the shin and a merkha under the lamed. \n                           BHL Appendix A has a patah under the shin. \n                </p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2022.12.07 - Changes/2022.12.07 - Changes.xml?2022.09.01-12\">2022.12.07 - Changes.xml : 2022.09.01-12</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?m\">All \"This meteg is a merkha in other texts.\" ('m') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "2Kings.9.17.19-t.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2022.12.07 - Changes.xml, date: 2022.09.01, number: 12 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Kings_2 9:17.19</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Kings_2 9:17.19</h1>\n  <h2>Replace sheva on shin with patah. Add 't' note. \n                         Replace merkha on lamed with meteg. Add 'm' note.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2022.12.07 - Changes/images/2022.09.01/12-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The vowel under the shin is hard to determine. \n                      A patah is a better fit than a sheva. \n                </p>\n  <p>\n                      A blob emerges from the top of the lamed of a word on the following line; \n                          word 22 of this verse. \n                      The blob might be considered in determining the markings on the shin of this word, word 19. \n                      There is a similar blob emerging from the lamed of the 5-th word of this verse. \n                      Consequently, the blob is considered to be an odd part of the lamed of word 22 \n                          and not part of the markings on the shin of word 19.\n                </p>\n  <p>The BHL has a hataf patah under the shin and a merkha under the lamed. \n                           BHL Appendix A has a patah under the shin. \n                </p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2022.12.07 - Changes/2022.12.07 - Changes.xml?2022.09.01-12\">2022.12.07 - Changes.xml : 2022.09.01-12</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>"
}
